Theorem RL-4: edge-specific decs on CFG edges; Jump-argument ownership-transfer exemption

  Preconditions:
    - RL-4 governs edge-specific RcDec emission per Annex E §AIMS RC
      Emission: "An OWNED non-scalar variable alive at block exit but dead
      at the successor entry SHALL receive a dec on that specific CFG edge.
      Jump argument exemption: variables passed as Jump args transfer
      ownership to the successor block param — NOT dead at successor entry
      (the block param IS the successor's name). Borrowed variables do NOT
      receive decs."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - Shipped site: emit_rc/edge_cleanup.rs::emit_edge_cleanup, called at
      the end of realize/mod.rs::realize_rc_reuse Phase 1. Edge decs are
      emitted pre-merge (Step 5) because they are position-keyed against the
      pre-merge CFG (Annex E §AIMS PL-3).
    - The Jump-arg exemption pairs with RL-2: a value passed as a Jump arg
      is an ownership-transferring use (per emit_rc/helpers.rs
      is_ownership_transfer), so neither RL-2 nor RL-4 emits a dec; the
      successor block param inherits the RC obligation.
    - Merge-point filtering (Annex E §AIMS.9
      project_alias_sources): the CFG-merge demand union is an
      over-approximation; emission filters so a variable live on only one
      predecessor path receives its dec on that specific edge, not at the
      merge block.

  Soundness property:
    Forall owned non-scalar value v and forall CFG edge (B -> S) where v is
    live at B's exit:

      (P1) Edge-dec decision: RL-4 emits an edge dec on (B -> S) iff
           (Access(v) = Owned AND NOT is_scalar(v) AND v live at B's exit
           AND v dead at S's entry AND v is NOT passed as a Jump arg on the
           edge). Borrowed values, scalars, still-live values, and Jump args
           do not receive edge decs.

      (P2) RC-count preservation across edges: a value that dies across an
           edge is released exactly once (by the edge dec) UNLESS it is a
           Jump arg, in which case ownership transfers to the successor
           block param (a handoff, no dec). The net reference count returns
           to 0 with no double-release on the transfer path.

    RL-4 refines plain ARC's scope-based dec placement by emitting the dec
    on the exact CFG edge where the value dies, and by exempting Jump args
    (whose ownership transfers to the block param) — preserving the same
    balance while avoiding both a leak (no dec on the dying edge) and a
    double-free (dec on the transfer edge).

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine.

    Part (P1) — edge-dec decision grid:

      The verifier enumerates an edge-decision grid and asserts RL-4's
      emit decision equals (Owned AND non-scalar AND live-at-exit AND
      dead-at-succ AND NOT jump-arg) on every row:
        owned_dead_across_edge_emits -> emit edge dec
        jump_arg_exempt_no_edge_dec -> NO dec (ownership transfers to the
                                          successor block param)
        borrowed_no_edge_dec -> NO dec (caller manages)
        live_at_succ_no_edge_dec -> NO dec (dec'd later)
        scalar_no_edge_dec -> NO dec (no RC)
      Coverage gate: 5 decisions (1 emit + 4 suppressed). A divergence fails
      the proof.

    Part (P2) — RC-count preservation (balance ledger):

      Sound lifecycles discharged (net = 0):
        dead_across_edge_balanced — alloc, edge dec releases the reference.
        jump_arg_transfer_balanced — alloc, ownership transfers to the
                                     successor block param (handoff, no dec).

    Negative-direction witness (REJECTED):
      NEG_edge_dec_on_jump_arg_double_free — RL-4 wrongly failing the
                                             Jump-arg exemption (emitting
                                             BOTH an edge dec AND the
                                             ownership transfer): net = -1
                                             (double-free). Rejected.
      Coverage gate: 3 ledger cases (2 sound + 1 negative witness).

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl4_edge_specific_decs;
        edge-dec decision grid + RC-balance ledger with the Jump-arg
        exemption; emits Fail on a decision divergence or a balance
        violation)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest
        RL row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 rc_counting engine discharges RL-4 via (P1) the edge-dec decision grid (1 emit + 4 suppressed: jump-arg / borrowed / live / scalar) and (P2) the RC-count-preservation balance ledger (2 sound lifecycles + 1 negative-direction witness showing an edge dec on a jump arg double-frees), grounded in the shipped emit_rc/edge_cleanup.rs emission site with the is_ownership_transfer Jump-arg exemption
